ARTICLES['work-home'].body=`<p class="studio-lead">We’re Cedar & Finch, an independent design studio in Lexington. We help people turn complicated ideas into identities, spaces, and websites that feel like them.</p><a class="studio-cta" href="#/article/designers">Meet our designers →</a><h2>Selected work</h2><div class="studio-grid"><a href="#/article/library-project"><h3>A new chapter</h3><p>Wayfinding & print · Neighborhood library</p></a><a href="#/article/garden-project"><h3>Room to grow</h3><p>Identity & digital · Community garden</p></a><a href="#/article/sponsor"><h3>Made for match day</h3><p>Event graphics · Riverdale Thunder</p></a></div><h2>A small studio. Many perspectives.</h2><p>We sketch around the same table, argue kindly about type, and make time to understand the people who will use what we create. Come explore our <a href="#/article/designers">team</a> and <a href="#/article/studio-journal">studio journal</a>.</p>`;
ARTICLES['dana-bio'].body=`<p class="studio-lead">Dana turns a pile of good ideas into a plan people can actually follow.</p><p>As project coordinator, she keeps schedules, print suppliers, and client conversations moving. She joined Cedar & Finch in 2022 after several years in Louisville, and still keeps a paper notebook beside her calendar.</p><p>“My favorite part is the moment someone sees their idea become a real thing. A sign, a booklet, a space—something they can point to and say, that’s ours.”</p><h2>Away from the studio</h2><p>Weekends tend to involve Casey’s soccer matches, Eli’s running commentary, and a library book Dana has promised herself she’ll finish. She volunteers with Riverdale Thunder and is the person most likely to bring far too many cupcakes. Her regular coffee order is an oat-milk latte; her studio mug has a chipped blue handle.</p><p>She collects old concert tickets, likes mystery novels, and believes a good project kickoff deserves actual conversation before anyone opens a spreadsheet.</p><p>Say hello: <strong>dana.selvin@cedarfinch.example</strong></p><p><a href="#/profile/dana">Dana’s Frame</a> · <a href="#/article/sponsor">Community Cup journal</a></p>`;
Object.assign(ARTICLES,{
 designers:{service:'work',title:'Different minds. Shared table.',date:'Meet our designers & project team',body:`<p class="studio-lead">The people who ask the extra question, notice the tiny detail, and stay curious.</p><div class="studio-grid"><a href="#/article/lena-bio"><h2>Lena Ortiz</h2><p>Brand & print designer</p><p>Type, texture, and the joy of making something by hand.</p></a><a href="#/article/dana-bio"><h2>Dana Selvin</h2><p>Project coordinator</p><p>A steady hand from the first conversation to the final delivery.</p></a><a href="#/article/sam-bio"><h2>Sam Reed</h2><p>Digital designer</p><p>Thoughtful websites for the people who use them.</p></a></div>`},
 'lena-bio':{service:'work',title:'Lena Ortiz',date:'Brand & print designer',body:`<p>Lena makes identities with a little personality and a lot of care. She grew up in Lexington and studied printmaking before joining the studio in 2021.</p><p>Outside work she teaches occasional lettering workshops at the arts center, hunts for old cookbooks, and posts her experiments as <a href="#/profile/lena">@lena.letters</a>.</p>`},
 'sam-bio':{service:'work',title:'Sam Reed',date:'Digital designer',body:`<p>Sam designs websites that work for busy people on ordinary devices. He joined Cedar & Finch in 2023 and keeps a shelf of board games by his desk.</p><p>Most Saturdays he volunteers at the community garden. His latest project is a seed-swap website. Find his notes on <a href="#/profile/sam">Frame</a>.</p>`},
 'studio-journal':{service:'work',title:'Notes from the studio',date:'Work, process & things we care about',body:`<h2><a href="#/article/sponsor">Made for match day</a></h2><p>Printed signs and a community effort at Riverdale Park.</p><h2><a href="#/article/library-project">A new chapter</a></h2><p>Helping visitors find their way.</p><h2><a href="#/article/garden-project">Room to grow</a></h2><p>A bright identity for a neighborhood project.</p>`},
 'library-project':{service:'work',title:'A new chapter',date:'Wayfinding · Print · 2026',image:'studio-gallery',body:`<p>The neighborhood library wanted its new readers’ room to feel welcoming before anyone reached the desk. Lena led the visual design; Dana coordinated the print schedule with library volunteer Ellis Morgan.</p><p>A flexible set of signs now connects books, events, and the people looking for them. The <a href="#/article/news-library">Lexington Ledger covered the reopening</a>.</p>`},
 'garden-project':{service:'work',title:'Room to grow',date:'Identity · Digital · 2026',image:'studio-desk',body:`<p>A shared garden needs more than a logo. Sam and Lena worked with volunteers on a seed-swap page, labels, and a simple noticeboard system.</p><p>The palette came from a box of seed packets. The type was chosen to be easy to read in bright sun. Sam still checks on the tomatoes every Saturday.</p>`},
 'news-cup':{service:'news',title:'Soccer, cupcakes, and a new set of goals',date:'24 October 2026 · Community · By Morgan Bell',image:'volunteers',body:`<p>Families filled Riverdale Park’s Field 3 on Saturday for the Thunder Community Cup, a fundraiser for youth team equipment. The event ran from 10 a.m. to 2 p.m., with matches, bake stalls, and plenty of sideline encouragement.</p><p>Volunteer coordinator Dana Selvin kept check-in moving with help from families and players. Casey Selvin, who wears number 7 for Riverdale Thunder, helped at the welcome table before joining her teammates.</p><p>Coach Kai Morgan praised the volunteers. “The kids remember the games, but it takes a lot of people to make a day like this happen.”</p><p>Cedar & Finch supplied the printed signs. Staff member Lena Ortiz said the wind provided an unexpected test of their mounting tape.</p><p>Priya Shah, a Riverdale yearbook photographer, captured the day alongside club photographers. More photos and the original event image are available in the <a href="#/article/recap">club’s photo recap</a>.</p><p>The organizers are wrapping up supply receipts this week; details are on the <a href="#/club">club website</a>.</p>`},
 'news-library':{service:'news',title:'Library readers’ room opens its doors',date:'22 October 2026 · Neighborhoods · By Morgan Bell',image:'studio-gallery',body:`<p>A brighter readers’ room welcomed visitors this week with new signs and a growing local-history shelf. Volunteer Ellis Morgan has been sorting donated photographs for a Sunday neighborhood walk.</p><p>The wayfinding was developed with <a href="#/work">Cedar & Finch</a>. Designer Lena Ortiz said the team tested the lettering from across the room before approving the final prints.</p><p>The history walk begins at the library steps Sunday at 10 a.m. Comfortable shoes are recommended.</p>`},
 'news-bikes':{service:'news',title:'A second life for well-loved bicycles',date:'24 October 2026 · Neighborhoods · By Jules Park',image:'corey-shop',body:`<p>At Spoke & Wrench, a neighborhood bicycle repair shop in Lexington, Corey Selvin spent Saturday morning working through squeaky brakes, punctured tires, and a stubborn bell on the library’s bike.</p><p>The workshop has bicycles on repair stands, a wall of hand tools, and racks of replacement tires. Selvin checks each repair before the bike leaves the shop.</p><p>“Sometimes a small adjustment makes a bike feel completely different,” he said. Between repairs, he shows customers how to check tire pressure and spot worn brake pads.</p><p>Find community updates on <a href="#/profile/corey">Corey’s public profile</a>.</p>`},
 'news-theatre':{service:'news',title:'Behind the curtain at Lafayette',date:'23 October 2026 · Arts · By Jules Park',body:`<p>Student stage crews are preparing for opening night next Friday. Casey Stevens, a senior, has spent the week painting scenery while the cast rehearses.</p><p>“The doors look real, but absolutely none of them open,” Stevens said. Lighting student Robin Hale says the final cues will be ready by Monday.</p><p>More backstage notes from <a href="#/profile/stevens">Casey Stevens</a>.</p>`},
 'news-market':{service:'news',title:'Autumn market makes room for local makers',date:'20 October 2026 · Arts · By Morgan Bell',body:`<p>Ceramicist June Ellis and woodworker Nolan Price will join more than twenty stallholders at next month’s autumn makers market.</p><p>Organizer Amira Cole is still looking for volunteers to help carry tables. Visitors can expect handmade bowls, paper goods, and a repair demonstration. The market is unrelated to this weekend’s soccer fundraiser.</p>`},
 'news-road':{service:'news',title:'Bridge resurfacing changes Monday bus route',date:'25 October 2026 · City desk · By Jules Park',body:`<p>Crews will resurface the pedestrian bridge beside Westbrook Green beginning Monday. The adjacent bus stop will move one block east for two days.</p><p>City spokesperson Ren Wallace said access to nearby businesses will remain open. Cyclists are asked to dismount on the temporary shared path.</p>`}
});
